Q: How can I position one element below another? A: <p>just give <code>position : relative</code> to second <code>div</code> and <code>top:315px</code> or what ever you want</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.first{
     width:70%;
     height:300px;
     position:absolute;
     border:1px solid red;
 }
.second{
    border:2px solid blue;
    width:40%;
    height:200px;
    position: relative;
    top: 315px;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;html&gt;
&lt;head&gt;

&lt;/head&gt;
&lt;body&gt;
&lt;div class="first"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="second"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/head&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
